# env.example — Oxford Command Center environment template
#
#   Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item env.example .env
#   bash:                cp env.example .env
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL unless marked REQUIRED. Every key is commented out; each one
# either has a working default (shown) or disables a feature when unset. Uncomment only what
# you need — an empty-but-present key is NOT the same as an absent one for some readers.
#
# .env is gitignored. NEVER commit real values, and never paste a secret into THIS file —
# it IS tracked. Keys only.
#
# Working in a git worktree? Use worktree-env.example instead (WAREHOUSE_DB must point at a
# per-worktree file — one SQLite writer at a time; see CLAUDE.md §5).

# ── REQUIRED: the two live data sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Master Workbook IS the company brain (Spine A). Defaults to the OneDrive path in
# server/config.ts; set only if the file moved.
# WORKBOOK_PATH=

# Oxford Edge market dataset directory (Acquisitions › Edge, read-only). Holds markets.json, which is
# written ONLY by the upstream oxford-edge pipeline. Defaults to the OneDrive path in
# server/edge/config.ts (edgeDir()); set only if the folder moved or on another machine.
# OXFORD_EDGE_DIR=

# Root of the lease/document corpus for the RAG index (npm run index:docs).
# DOCUMENTS_DIR=

# Property P&L workbooks the warehouse backfill ingests (Spine B).
# FINANCIALS_DIR=

# QuickBooks Desktop CSV export (Desktop only — the QBO MCP is structurally incompatible).
# QUICKBOOKS_CSV=

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude API key — AI narrative briefings, OM extraction.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# FRED (St. Louis Fed) API key — macro series + state unemployment.
# FRED_API_KEY=

# Notion internal integration token — Tenant DB + Acquisition Pipeline sync.
# NOTION_TOKEN=

# HubSpot PRIVATE APP access token, scope `crm.objects.deals.read` ONLY.
# Powers POST /acq/sync/hubspot (server/warehouse/acq-hubspot-sync.ts) — read-only from
# HubSpot, writes only local acq_candidates. NOT a Personal Access Key (that is for the `hs`
# CLI) and NOT an OAuth/public app (no refresh flow exists in this code).
# HUBSPOT_TOKEN=

# Microsoft Graph app registration (see the graph-app-registration skill). CLIENT_SECRET
# expires every 24 months. GRAPH_TOKEN is a pre-minted bearer token used only as a test seam.
# GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=
# GRAPH_TENANT_ID=
# GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GRAPH_USER=
# GRAPH_TOKEN=

# ── Notion targets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTION_TENANT_DB=b12f4cfda995475583416435ae8173b4
# NOTION_DEALS_DB=46c8a5c6-8b37-4c53-a10d-0f55c97613e5
# NOTION_DEALS_ID_PROP=Deal ID
# NOTION_VERSION=2025-09-03
# Data-source ids (Notion 2025-09-03 API). Resolved from the DB id when unset.
# NOTION_TENANT_DATA_SOURCE=
# NOTION_DEALS_DATA_SOURCE=
# Extra confidentiality name patterns applied to synced Notion deals.
# NOTION_CONFIDENTIAL_NAME_PATTERNS=
# NOTION_DEALS_NAME_ALIASES=

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRAIN_SERVER_PORT=8911          # a bare SERVER_PORT is ignored by everything
# Extra `Host` authorities the API answers to, comma-separated (server/host-guard.ts, OI-050).
# localhost:<port> and 127.0.0.1:<port> are always allowed; everything else is 403'd as a
# DNS-rebinding defense. Needed ONLY for the Cloudflare-tunnel deployment, where cloudflared
# forwards the public hostname as Host (alternative: set httpHostHeader in the tunnel ingress).
# A non-empty BRAIN_ALLOWED_HOSTS REQUIRES ACCESS_REQUIRE=1 (and the three ACCESS_* values below), or the
# server refuses to start (server/access-authz.ts): a tunnel must never serve the API unauthenticated.
# The one exception is BRAIN_HOST_AUTH=tailnet (below).
# BRAIN_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Host-auth mode for the extra hosts. Unset or empty = the rule above. Exactly `tailnet` = the Tailscale
# Serve deployment: extra hosts may run WITHOUT ACCESS_REQUIRE=1, but ONLY if every one is a *.ts.net name
# (whole-label suffix match: ts.net.evil.com, evilts.net or a bare ts.net still refuse to start). The
# tailnet ACL is then the authorization boundary (logged once at startup), so Tailscale Funnel must stay
# off for the node. tailnet + ACCESS_REQUIRE=1 is allowed and enforces Cloudflare Access as well. Any
# other value ('Tailnet', ' tailnet', 'access', ...) refuses to start.
# BRAIN_HOST_AUTH=tailnet
# Cloudflare Access verification of the Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion (server/access-authz.ts; same rule as the
# edge, functions/_shared/access-identity.ts): unset, empty or 0 = off (local dev); 1 = on; ANY other
# value refuses to start. With ACCESS_REQUIRE=1 the three values below are required.
# ACCESS_REQUIRE=1
# ACCESS_ISSUER=https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# ACCESS_AUD=
# ACCESS_ALLOWLIST=                # comma-separated emails
# ORA_SERVER=http://localhost:3000
# ORA_PYTHON=python               # interpreter for the AR PDF extractor

# ── Data paths (all default under data/, all gitignored) ──────────────────────────────────
# WAREHOUSE_DB=data/warehouse/finance.sqlite
# WAREHOUSE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS=      # SQLite busy timeout; raise under heavy concurrent access
# SNAPSHOT_PATH=data/snapshots/portfolio.json   # TRACKED file — auto-committed by the refresh tasks
# OVERLAY_PATH=data/overlay.json  # live user mutations; irreplaceable (CLAUDE.md §9)
# DOC_INDEX_PATH=data/doc-index.sqlite
# AR_INBOX=data/ar/inbox          # review-queue.json + processed/ derive from its parent
# AR_MAPPING_CACHE=data/ar-mapping-cache.json
# ALERT_INBOX_PATH=data/alert-inbox.json
# ALERT_STATE_PATH=data/alert-state.json
# BRIEF_HEALTH_PATH=data/brief-health.json
# BRIEF_OUTBOX_DIR=data/outbox

# ── Document indexing (npm run index:docs) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DOCUMENTS_INCLUDE_DIRS=         # fail-closed top-level allowlist
# DOCUMENTS_EXCLUDE=
# DOCUMENTS_PATH_INCLUDE=
# DOCUMENTS_DROP_NONLEASE=
# DOCUMENTS_NONLEASE_PATTERNS=
# DOCUMENTS_MAX_FILES=
# DOCUMENTS_MAX_DEPTH=
# DOCUMENTS_MAX_FILE_MB=
# DOCUMENTS_MAX_CHUNKS_PER_DOC=
# DOCUMENTS_EMBED_BATCH=
# DOCUMENTS_EMBED_LIMIT=
# DOCUMENTS_ALLOW_UNSCOPED=1      # '1' disables the allowlist — indexes EVERYTHING under
                                  # DOCUMENTS_DIR. Leave unset in normal use.

# ── Daily brief ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRIEF_ENABLED=1                 # '1' arms the brief; anything else leaves it inert
# BRIEF_SEND_SCRIPT=_shared/send-via-outlook.ps1   # Outlook COM is the sole send path
# BRIEF_DASHBOARD_URL=https://ora-command-center.pages.dev

# ── AI model selection ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=               # low | medium | high | max
# OM_EXTRACT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001   # deliberately separate from ANTHROPIC_MODEL

# ── Confidentiality gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fails CLOSED when unreadable, by design. The test suite points this at a synthetic fixture.
# CONFIDENTIAL_TERMS_PATH=
# CONFIDENTIAL_TERMS_ALLOW_PLACEHOLDER=
# MIRROR_INCLUDE_CONFIDENTIAL=1   # '1' bakes confidential deals into the public mirror.
                                  # Do NOT set for any deployed mirror (invariant 3).

# ── Escape hatches / test seams (normally leave unset) ────────────────────────────────────
# REPORT_DATE=                    # pins "today" for deterministic day-count math
# WORKBOOK_AS_OF=2026-06-01       # workbook DATA month column; NOT the report date
# ALERT_CONFIRM_CLEAR_RUNS=
# BRAIN_BAKE_SOURCE_URL=          # defaults to the local brain server
# REFUTE_BASE=

# ── Deliberately NOT listed ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GIT_SHA, ORA_CODE_VERSION, NODE_OPTIONS — injected by CI/tooling at build or run time (each
# falls back to 'dev' locally). Setting them in .env would pin a stale build stamp, so they are
# omitted on purpose rather than overlooked.

# Bootstrap escape hatch for a genuinely NEW install that has no data/overlay.json yet.
# Set to exactly "1" to let the snapshot writers proceed with an EMPTY overlay. Every run that
# honors it prints a loud warning, because the variable is sticky (it lives in this file, and the
# snapshot scheduled tasks copy .env into each run's worktree).
# It does NOT bypass a MISSING overlay file — bootstrapping takes both acts: create data/overlay.json
# containing {} AND set this. Leave it UNSET in any environment with real overlay data: with it set,
# a truncated or wrongly-pathed overlay silently zeroes tenantArrears / arBalances / renewalStages /
# dealComps / marketRents / noiBudgets in the written snapshot.
# ALLOW_EMPTY_OVERLAY=1
